# The replay cache is bytes, not text.
#
# Git normalises line endings on files it thinks are text, which rewrites them
# between the working tree and the object store. For ordinary source that is
# invisible and helpful. For this directory it is a silent corruption: the whole
# point of manifest.sha256 is that these files are byte-identical everywhere, and
# OCHA's population CSV ships with CRLF endings that git helpfully converted to
# LF on commit — changing the file's hash and failing CI on a clone that had
# never been touched by a human.
#
# Marking the cache as not-text stops git from having an opinion about its
# contents. Caught by the manifest doing exactly its job, which is the only
# reason this was a red build and not a demo that quietly stopped reproducing.
data/replay/cache/** -text -diff

# Committed binaries elsewhere.
*.pptx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
